1
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:21,720
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: The Budget Hearing of the Committee on Appropriations of the House Bill No. 10858,

2
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:29,300
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the Fiscal Year 2027 General Appropriation Bill, is hereby resumed.

3
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:43,250
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Committee Secretary, please acknowledge the members present and the resource persons present today.

4
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:55,470
Committee Secretary: Good afternoon, Your Honors. May we acknowledge the members present today? Deputy Majority Leader and Vice Chair Bong Teves, Vice Chair Emery Lollipop Uwano-Dizon,

5
00:00:56,110 --> 00:00:58,730
Committee Secretary: Vice Chair Maria Angela Garcia,

6
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:01,050
Committee Secretary: Representative

7
00:01:01,050 --> 00:01:07,590
Committee Secretary: Robert Nezal, Representative Dada Ismula, Representative Alexander Pimentel.

8
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:16,270
Committee Secretary: And with us in the room, we have Vice Chair Dante Garcia and Vice Chair Ompong Ordanez.

9
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:24,570
Committee Secretary: We also acknowledge our guests from the Civil Service Commission, headed by Chairperson

10
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:30,730
Committee Secretary: Marilyn Villap, Commissioner Ryan Alvin Acosta, Commissioner Luis,

11
00:01:32,010 --> 00:01:35,890
Committee Secretary: Minister y Menrano Pangulayan,

12
00:01:38,870 --> 00:01:43,890
Committee Secretary: Assistant Commissioner Arielle Ronquillo, Assistant Commissioner Judith Dongalo Chicano,

13
00:01:44,790 --> 00:01:51,310
Committee Secretary: Assistant Commissioner Marlon Lim, Career Executive Service Board Chairperson Orduja Alvarado,

14
00:01:53,050 --> 00:01:58,750
Committee Secretary: MCSB Executive Director María Marcy Corsare Valies Peros,

15
00:01:58,750 --> 00:02:00,770
Committee Secretary: and we have our guest from the Civil Society

16
00:02:00,770 --> 00:02:09,870
Committee Secretary: Organization, from the Philippine Association of Agriculturists, Mr. Al-Christian Hilario.

17
00:02:10,490 --> 00:02:11,230
Committee Secretary: That's all, Your Honor.

18
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:16,080
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you, Sec.

19
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:25,860
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Honorable members, team colleagues, good afternoon.

20
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:34,620
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: I would like to welcome everyone to this budget hearing of the Civil Service Commission,

21
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:44,280
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: including the Career Executive Service Board, headed by Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap.

22
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:54,520
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: As the agency responsible for managing and strengthening the government's human resources,

23
00:02:56,060 --> 00:03:03,180
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the CSC recognizes the need to continuously modernize its systems

24
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:07,180
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and processes. Digital transformation

25
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:11,460
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Digital transformation is no longer simply an option.

26
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:22,000
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: It is essential to providing faster, more efficient, and more accessible government services.

27
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:33,980
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: For fiscal year 2027, the CSC is proposing a total budget of 3.89 billion.

28
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:36,980
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: This represents

29
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:48,140
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: an increase of 1.14 billion, or 41.4% from the fiscal year 2026

30
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:53,420
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: approved budget of 2.89 billion.

31
00:03:54,200 --> 00:04:03,160
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: A significant portion of this proposed increase, amounting to $1.453 billion,

32
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:07,160
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: is extended for the implementation...

33
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:13,900
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: of the Philippine Civil Service Modernization Project, PCSMP,

34
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:25,540
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: a parent-assisted project that will support the modernization of our human resource system.

35
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:35,660
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Among its key initiatives are the rollout of Prime Embedded Systems Governance, ESG,

36
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:45,820
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the HRMIS payroll system, and the development of a national learning management system.

37
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:54,680
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: These initiatives are intended to make human resource services more efficient,

38
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:58,260
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: accessible, and responsive,

39
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:04,740
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: while also improving the delivery of services to government employees,

40
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:06,240
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and the public.

41
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:15,700
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: I will enable the CAC to maintain reliable, secure, and continuous operation

42
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:20,040
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: while advancing the modernization of the civil service.

43
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:24,080
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: With the continued trust and support of Congress,

44
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:27,940
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: the Civil Service Commission will be better positioned

45
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:33,180
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: to lead the modernization of human resource governance

46
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:34,940
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: in the Philippine bureaucracy,

47
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:40,660
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and contribute to a more efficient, responsive,

48
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:43,660
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and citizen-centered government.

49
00:05:43,660 --> 00:05:52,380
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you very much, and we look forward to a productive and meaningful discussion.

50
00:05:52,380 --> 00:06:07,420
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Chairperson Marilyn Yap, you may now proceed with your presentation.

51
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:11,880
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Hello.

52
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:16,880
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Deputy Majority Leader and Appropriations Committee Vice Chairperson,

53
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:48,020
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Representative Dada Kiram Pismula, Representative Emery Lollipop Uano Dizon, Representative Angela Garcia, Representative Dante Garcia, Representative Choboy Aquino, and all our honorable representatives who are attending this meeting online.

54
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:50,480
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Magandang hapon po sa ating lahat.

55
00:06:50,480 --> 00:07:15,080
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: We are pleased to present this afternoon the proposed 2027 budget of the Civil Service Commission along with highlights of our accomplishments for the year 2024 to the first semester 2025 and up to the first semester of 2026 and including our targets for 2027.

56
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:20,080
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Ang amin pong proposed budget ay maglalahad ng mga programa upang panaginipan.

57
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:24,000
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Magtuloy naming mapagbuti ang pagtupad ng aming mandato.

58
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:45,260
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Nasa slide po ngayon ang mandato ng Civil Service Commission to be the central personal agency of the government tasked to establish a career service and adopt measures to promote moral efficiency, integrity, responsiveness, progressiveness, and courtesy in the civil service.

59
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:50,060
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: It is also tasked, our commission is also tasked to strengthen the merit.

60
00:07:50,480 --> 00:08:04,840
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and reward system, integrate all human resource development programs for all levels and ranks, and institutionalize a management climate in government conducive to public accountability.

61
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:21,680
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Sa kanyang 2026 State of the Nation address, nanawagan ang Pangulong Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. na ipagpatuloy natin ang nasimulan nating mga gawain upang maibigay sa ating mga kababayan,

62
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:24,180
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: ang pansang karapatdapat sa kanila.

63
00:08:24,180 --> 00:08:36,780
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Ito ay nagsisilbing inspirasyon para sa amin para patuloy naming pagsikapan at pagbutihin ang aming mga programa upang ang pamahalaan ay patuloy na maging karapatdapat

64
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:41,120
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: sa pagtitiwala ng pamamayan.

65
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:50,040
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Sa ngayon po, as of June 2026 the Philippine Civil Service Workforce is more than 2.25 million strong,

66
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:59,780
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: consisting of 2.02 million career professionals and 232,770-plus non-career professionals.

67
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:05,060
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Ito po ang distribution across sectors ng ating career and non-career professionals,

68
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:10,080
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: sectors meaning the national government agencies, the state universities and colleges,

69
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:14,380
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: local government units, government-owned and controlled corporations,

70
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:17,060
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: kasama na po ang mga local water districts.

71
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:20,860
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Pag-tignan niyo po ang mga datos natin,

72
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:26,060
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: 73.6% of career professionals work in national government agencies,

73
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:31,300
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: while 18.5% work in local government units.

74
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:39,480
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: On the other hand, 60.6% of non-career professionals work in LGUs or local government units,

75
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:44,440
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: while only 29.7% work in national government agencies.

76
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,280
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: In addition,

77
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:59,600
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: there are also workers in the government workforce which are called job order and contract of service workers.

78
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:05,520
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Today, there are more than 1 million job order and contract of service workers in government.

79
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:12,660
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: The majority of JOs and COs are in local government units,

80
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:16,940
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: while only 22.14% are in national government.

81
00:10:17,060 --> 00:10:24,220
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: So, all together, the government workforce is more than 3.29 million,

82
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:29,100
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: composed of 2.021 million professionals,

83
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:33,660
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: 232,770 plus non-career professionals,

84
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:41,920
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and 1,038,204 job order and contract of service workers.

85
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:46,920
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Ang ating civil service workforce,

86
00:10:47,060 --> 00:10:51,060
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: ay ito po ang aming workforce sa civil service.

87
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:57,060
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: The CSC has only a total personnel allocation of 1,690 positions.

88
00:10:57,520 --> 00:11:00,980
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Of this number, 1,541 are filled,

89
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:04,280
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: consisting of 1,260 career employees,

90
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,340
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: 49 career employees,

91
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:10,740
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and 241 JOs and contracts of service workers.

92
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:16,760
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: 149 positions in our agency remain unfilled or vacant.

93
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:20,060
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Despite our nationwide mandate,

94
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:24,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: there is only one civil service second-level and up employee

95
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:29,020
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: for every 3,199 government workers.

96
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:34,440
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: In comparison, COA has 13,310 personnel,

97
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,640
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: COMELEC has 6,971,

98
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:43,660
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and the CSC has only a total personnel allocation of 1,690.

99
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:48,580
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Our proposed fiscal year 2027 budget

100
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:52,660
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: embodies our commitment to strengthen the civil service

101
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:55,220
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: through our three program pillars,

102
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,640
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: namely human resource governance,

103
00:11:58,140 --> 00:12:00,540
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: professionalization and workplace cooperation,

104
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:03,300
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and administrative justice.

105
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:05,900
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: For human resource governance,

106
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:09,600
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: ang una pong sub-program,

107
00:12:12,350 --> 00:12:14,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: ang human resource governance,

108
00:12:14,910 --> 00:12:16,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: ay ito po ang mga policy reforms

109
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:20,370
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: that have been implemented for the period mentioned earlier.

110
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:26,170
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: The CSC continues to implement the 2025 Omnibus Rules and Appointments

111
00:12:26,170 --> 00:12:29,550
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and other human resource actions, or ORA-ORA,

112
00:12:29,550 --> 00:12:32,950
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: which now allows for digital signatures to be affixed

113
00:12:32,950 --> 00:12:35,950
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: on Civil Service Commission records.

114
00:12:35,950 --> 00:12:39,830
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Online oath-taking and online submission of appointments

115
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:41,830
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: are also already allowed.

116
00:12:41,830 --> 00:12:46,590
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: This is part of the shift that is integral

117
00:12:46,590 --> 00:12:49,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: to our moves for digital transformation in the Commission.

118
00:12:49,750 --> 00:12:53,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: We also issued the 2025 Rules and Administrative Cases

119
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:54,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: in the Civil Service

120
00:12:54,750 --> 00:12:57,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and the 2025 Omnibus Rules and SALN.

121
00:12:57,750 --> 00:13:02,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: And today, we now allow digital signatures

122
00:13:02,750 --> 00:13:06,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: in terms of cases, pati-oath-taking, digital na rin po.

123
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:09,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: And then, the Omnibus Rules and SALN

124
00:13:09,750 --> 00:13:13,750
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: provides for digital SALN forms, submission online

125
00:13:13,750 --> 00:13:19,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: of statement of assets, liabilities, and net worth.

126
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: We also expanded the project

127
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:25,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: with preferential ratings for qualified job orders,

128
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:29,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: contract of service, and other covered government workers.

129
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:32,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Preferential ratings were provided for,

130
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:34,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: not only for JOs and COs,

131
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:37,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: but also for military and uniformed personnel

132
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:40,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and overseas Filipino workers.

133
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:43,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: In addition, the Commission has approved the reduction

134
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:46,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: of the experience requirement for JOs and COs

135
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:49,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: from the 10 years in previous years

136
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: to five years.

137
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:53,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: The Commission has also approved the reduction

138
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:55,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: of the experience in government service.

139
00:13:55,320 --> 00:14:01,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: We also have a policy to enable K-12 graduates

140
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:05,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: to qualify for first-level positions in government.

141
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:08,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: We also granted, pursuant to the law,

142
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:10,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: an SK autonomy,

143
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:14,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: the grant of eligibility to Sangguniang Kabataan officials.

144
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:18,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: The latest is the Wellness Leave Policy

145
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:20,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and the Gambling Prohibition Policy.

146
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:23,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: The Wellness Leave Policy gives five days

147
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:26,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: wellness leave to all government employees,

148
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:29,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and the Gambling Prohibition Policy inhibits

149
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:32,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: or prescribes any form of gambling

150
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:34,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: among government employees,

151
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:37,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: whether this be on-site or online.

152
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:39,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: We are also pursuing major reforms

153
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:41,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: to modernize the civil service.

154
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:44,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: These include the review and overhaul

155
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:46,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: of our qualification standards,

156
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: which are more than 30 years old

157
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:50,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and are no longer applicable

158
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:53,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: to the present requirements of the government service.

159
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:55,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: This program is being undertaken

160
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: with the University of the Philippines

161
00:14:57,320 --> 00:15:00,320
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: National College of Public Administration

162
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:07,980
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: And the focus is in shifting qualification standards to competency-based standards.

163
00:15:07,980 --> 00:15:18,560
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: We are also reviewing our civil service examinations with the possible shift also of the civil

164
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:25,160
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: service examinations from aptitude-based exams to competency-based examinations.

165
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:29,940
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: We are also laying the groundwork for the establishment of the National Civil Service

166
00:15:29,940 --> 00:15:36,200
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Leadership and Management Development Center at New Clark City with the BASIS Conversion

167
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,940
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Development Authority.

168
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:48,820
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: Sa ating Prime HRM, which is a major program on human resource governance, the Prime HRM

169
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:55,120
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: aims to improve public sector HR systems, namely recruitment, selection, and placement,

170
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:56,160
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: placement, selection, and placement, career, performance management, learning and development,

171
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,220
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: and rewards and recognition.

172
00:15:57,220 --> 00:16:05,840
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: 477 HRM systems were recognized in 2024, increasing to 517 in 2025.

173
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:13,140
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: For the first semester of 2026, 193 HRM systems have already been recognized.

174
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:20,160
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: For accreditation, 134 agencies were accredited in 2024.

175
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:25,120
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: 193 in 2020 and three years in between.

176
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:31,960
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: As of June 2026, 54 agencies have been accredited.

177
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:38,820
CSC Chairperson Marilyn B. Yap: For prime HRM awards, these are the bronze, silver, and gold awards, 128 agencies were

178
